{"type": "FeatureCollection", "metadata": {"note": "The Gulf Breeze, a short-lived Amtrak train (not a private-railroad-era service like most of this map's other entries): a daily southbound section of the Crescent that split off at Birmingham, AL and ran 275 miles further to Mobile via seven Alabama stations, jointly funded by Amtrak and the state of Alabama (the state paying roughly $1.3 million/year). It ran October 27 1989 - April 1 1995, discontinued in Amtrak's December 1994 cost-cutting round and replaced by a bus connection; FY1994 ridership was just 7,737 passengers. The New York-Birmingham portion reuses amtrak.geojson's current 'Crescent' GTFS shape for that shared trackage (still the same route the Crescent runs today); the Birmingham-Mobile extension is a real-town waypoint approximation of the seven-station list (Birmingham-Montgomery-Greenville-Evergreen-Brewton-Atmore-Bay Minette-Mobile), straight-line segments between those documented stations, NOT digitized from period track maps.", "sources": ["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gulf_Breeze_(train) (full station list with mileposts; service Oct 27 1989-Apr 1 1995; discontinued in Amtrak's Dec 1994 cuts, replaced by bus; joint Amtrak/Alabama funding ~$1.3M/year state share; FY1994 ridership 7,737)"], "not_yet_sourced": "Exact frequency (modeled here as one daily round trip, matching the 'daily passenger train' description); whether the train used distinct equipment or was truly through-cars off the Crescent.", "line_label_audit": "2026-08-24: line labels normalised repo-wide to \"<operating company>: <line name>\" -- the company's common display name (legal suffixes dropped), then the line as a passenger would have known it, or its two terminals where the line carried no advertised name. Long intermediate station lists were reduced to endpoints. For features spanning several operators the company shown is the one that ran the line for most of its drawn years. See CLAUDE.md Rule 6."}, "features": [{"type": "Feature", "properties": {"company": "Amtrak", "line": "Amtrak: Gulf Breeze", "id": "amtrak-gulf-breeze", "color": "#1c4e80", "mode": "intercity_rail", "avg_speed_kmh": 75, "speed_source": "estimated, consistent with other early-1990s Amtrak long-distance service; unsourced", "segments": [{"start": 1989, "end": 1995, "headway_min": 1440, "note": "Ran as a daily section of the Crescent, splitting off at Birmingham for an additional 275 miles to Mobile via Montgomery, Greenville, Evergreen, Brewton, Atmore, and Bay Minette; jointly funded by Amtrak and the state of Alabama; discontinued Apr 1 1995 in Amtrak's Dec 1994 cost-cutting round and replaced by bus service", "sources": ["NOT SOURCED AT SEGMENT LEVEL: the references below cover this line, but nothing has been checked specifically against this segment's start year, end year or service. Treat the dates and the headway as unverified. Supporting references for the line:", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gulf_Breeze_(train"]}], "geometry_repairs": [{"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-88.0399, 30.6954], "to": [-87.7728, 30.8827], "chord_mi": 19.75, "traced_mi": 23.84, "snap_m": [99, 170], "bridged_mi": 0.0, "osm_lines": ["CSX M&M Subdivision (22.85 mi)", "CSX NO&M Subdivision (0.93 mi)", "(rail) (0.06 mi)"], "method": "Overpass rail graph, 8.0 km corridor, Dijkstra, simplified to 3.0 m"}, {"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-87.7728, 30.8827], "to": [-87.4922, 31.0227], "chord_mi": 18.42, "traced_mi": 20.88, "snap_m": [170, 164], "bridged_mi": 0.0, "osm_lines": ["CSX M&M Subdivision (20.88 mi)"], "method": "Overpass rail graph, 8.0 km corridor, Dijkstra, simplified to 3.0 m"}, {"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-87.0705, 31.1149], "to": [-86.953, 31.4321], "chord_mi": 22.88, "traced_mi": 24.37, "snap_m": [675, 256], "bridged_mi": 0.0, "osm_lines": ["CSX M&M Subdivision (24.37 mi)"], "method": "Overpass rail graph, 8.0 km corridor, Dijkstra, simplified to 3.0 m"}, {"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-77.77175, 38.56648], "to": [-